  partName: Blade (3)
  description: The Blade (3) is a key component of the jet engine's turbine section,
    where it extracts energy from the hot gases produced by combustion and converts
    it into mechanical energy to drive the engine's compressor. Its unique shape
    and size allow it to withstand the extreme temperatures and stresses encountered
    in this section, making it a critical part of the engine's overall performance.
    Interestingly, the Blade (3) is often designed with a specialized cooling system
    to prevent overheating and maintain its structural integrity.
